>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `del_looper`

``` hol4
simpLib.del_looper : string -> simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes a named looper from a simpset.

`del_looper name ss` removes the looper `name` added by `add_looper`,
`set_looper` or `looper_ss`. Split loopers are removed with `del_split`.

### Failure

Never fails. If there is no looper `name`, a warning is printed and `ss`
is returned.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpLib.add_looper ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
     boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val ss' = simpLib.del_looper "conj" ss;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_looper`](#simpLib.add_looper),
[`simpLib.del_split`](#simpLib.del_split).
